Field	Value
Report	Supplier Lead-Time Report — DER Program Equipment (RTUs & POI reclosers)
Prepared by	Marcus Deele, SCADA/EMS Engineering
As of	06/30/2025
Scope	Utility-owned RTU and POI recloser procurement in support of in-scope DER interconnection commissionings (≥500 kW). Program-owned only; customer-side equipment excluded.
Current approved suppliers — RTU	Kelvraith Grid Systems, Inc. (approved supplier of record)
Current approved suppliers — POI recloser	Norstead Power Controls, LLC (approved supplier of record)
Quoted lead time — RTU	~8-month lead time from PO acknowledgement to delivery to Halston staging yard
Quoted lead time — POI recloser	~8-month lead time from PO acknowledgement to delivery to Halston staging yard
Lead-time framing	The ~8-month supplier lead time for RTUs and POI reclosers from the current approved suppliers, both device types, is a shortcoming of the current approved suppliers. Quoted intervals have not shortened materially through 2024–2025 despite repeated escalation with Kelvraith and Norstead account management.
Incoming — 08/2025	2 RTU + POI recloser sets arriving 08/2025 (one complete set per site allocation).
Incoming — 03/2026	Next delivery 03/2026 (aggregated shipment covering remaining committed orders).
Sites waiting on utility equipment	7 completed sites awaiting utility equipment (construction complete; RTU and/or POI recloser outstanding). See companion tracker for site-level detail.
Flag — grant-funded project	Grant-funded community project contracted in-service 09/30/2025 at risk. Alleron Community Solar Initiative — Rowan Hill (1.05 MW) requires RTU + POI recloser; only two sets land 08/2025 and the next window is 03/2026.
Related standards	TCS-02 §5 (≥500 kW → utility RTU + SCADA telemetry); DPS-07 §4.2 / DIS-01 §5 (POI recloser applicability); OG-17 (deployment sequencing of constrained utility equipment).
Companion files	DER-EQP-COMPL Completed_Sites_Awaiting_Equipment.xlsx (site-level roster); OG-17 Equipment Deployment Prioritization Guideline.
Narrative notes	
• The ~8-month lead time is quoted by both current approved suppliers and has been reconfirmed by Kelvraith (RTU) on 06/12/2025 and by Norstead (POI recloser) on 06/18/2025 against outstanding purchase orders.	
• Neither supplier has offered an expedite fee schedule that would compress the interval below ~8 months. Requests for partial shipments have been declined by both suppliers on the basis of factory build slotting.	
• Vendor qualification of alternative sources for equivalent RTUs and POI reclosers is in progress; see Tab 3.	
